            "content_sub_title": "Pallu Patari is part of the Nawalgaria Collective, a family-led textile business established in 1990",
            "content_description": "<br>Over four generations, our understanding of sarees has come from being closely involved in how they are sourced, chosen, and worn.\n<br><br>\nThe idea of Pallu Patari comes from something familiar — the patari.\nA space in every home where sarees are kept with care. Not all of them, but the ones that are worn often, valued over time, and chosen with intention.\n<br><br>\nThat thought guides how we build our collections.\n<br><br>\nWe work across different regions in India, bringing together sarees that strike a balance between fabric, design, and wearability. Each piece is selected keeping in mind how it feels, how it fits into a wardrobe, and how often it will actually be worn.\n<br><br>\nThe name reflects this approach.\n<br><br>\nThe pallu represents the detail and identity of a saree, while the patari stands for value and permanence. Together, they shape a collection that is thoughtful and relevant.\n<br><br>\nOur approach is consistent — careful selection, dependable quality, and pricing that is fair.\n<br><br>\nPallu Patari is not built on volume, but on choosing sarees that hold their place over time.\n<br><br>\nA Patari of Curated Sarees.",
